range bed level 0.18 0.3 the old synth bed as a haze: a cluster in the recording, so every partial is gathered onto C and G
range flame level 0 0.3 the old 'third' loop as flame: gathered onto C and G, so its flicker stays and its wrong notes go: the orb's reach
range embers level 0 0.12 the old 'root' loop as embers, gathered the same way: grows with the machine
range glow level 0.063 0.09 the ember glow: saws at C2 and C3, low-passed and driven warm, breathing slowly. The only bass.
range root level 0 0.08 C4: an FM voice (modulator an octave under: a growl)
range root fm_depth 0.3 2.2 the roughness: a rough, roaring flame at coherence 0, a clean one at 1
range third level 0 0.07 E4
range fifth level 0 0.07 G4
range seventh level 0 0.056 Bb4
range crackle level 0.3 1 fire crackle: an arc eight pops a second, dark, at random: louder with the pen's speed
range roar level 0.03 0.3 the blazing-fire recording: the pen's speed
range cloud level 0 0.3 the chord, growing with the number of motions; spells raise it and pick the chord
range cloud gather 0.5 1 a soft cluster while searching, the chord once every ratio is an integer
range fire level 0 0.3 the fire recording, on whenever the machine stirs (drive 0.12 lifts its body)
range fire cutoff 0.6 0.97 a low-pass the score opens: about 1.1 kHz while searching, about 8 kHz at a match, where the wood crackle comes through
bind stack cloud level 0 0.3
bind coherence cloud gather 0.5 1
bind radiance cloud reverb 0.3 0.7
bind stir fire level 0 0.3
bind score fire cutoff 0.6 0.97
bind stir glow level 0.09 0.063
bind orb.radius glow cutoff 0.38 0.55
bind orb.accel glow drive 0.25 0.45
bind stir bed level 0.3 0.18
bind orb.speed crackle level 0.3 1
bind orb.radius flame level 0 0.3
bind orb.curl flame cutoff 0.5 1
bind stack embers level 0 0.12
bind orb.radius embers cutoff 0.5 1
bind orb.speed roar level 0.03 0.3
bind orb.radius roar cutoff 0.6 0.95
bind tone.root root level 0 0.08
bind coherence root fm_depth 2.2 0.3
bind fit root shimmer 0.4 0
bind orb.radius root cutoff 0.4 0.85
bind tone.third third level 0 0.07
bind coherence third fm_depth 2.2 0.3
bind fit third shimmer 0.4 0
bind orb.radius third cutoff 0.4 0.85
bind tone.fifth fifth level 0 0.07
bind coherence fifth fm_depth 2.2 0.3
bind fit fifth shimmer 0.4 0
bind orb.radius fifth cutoff 0.4 0.85
bind tone.seventh seventh level 0 0.056
bind coherence seventh fm_depth 2.2 0.3
bind fit seventh shimmer 0.4 0
bind orb.radius seventh cutoff 0.4 0.85
bind orb.accel root drive 0.2 0.45
bind orb.accel fifth drive 0.2 0.45
bind hand.fit fire cutoff 0 0.25 rel
bind hand.fit fire level 0 0.1 rel
note pyretic v4 (2026-10-03). Why: measured, v3's pitched recordings were not on their notes. The bed is a cluster (C, B, F#, E, D#, ...), the 'third' loop
note sat on G#, E, D#, D, and the 'root' loop was mostly A and E with a little C. Here every note is an oscillator: exact, and one instrument.
note notes = four FM voices at C4 E4 G4 Bb4 (tone.*); in tune = the flame burns clean: the FM growl falls away with coherence (fm_depth 2.2 -> 0.3); fit steadies the pitch;
note a faint random flutter stays on each voice (flame). The orb's radius opens their filters, its acceleration drives the root, the fifth and the glow harder.
note Fire layers (oscillators alone were exact and generic): the three old synth loops return as haze (bed), flame and embers, each with every partial gathered
note onto C or G: their flicker and their noise are what read as fire, and neither needs their pitches. The blazing-fire recording and an arc crackle follow the pen's speed;
note the fire recording is on whenever the machine stirs, behind a low-pass that the score opens to 8 kHz (in the spells it stays open). cloud, one-shots and spells are v3's (their bed lines are gathered too).
note Reach hint: hand.fit (the reach of the component in hand against the recipe the stations point to) adds a little to one layer when it is right, and nothing otherwise; fit steadies the voices.
note Recipes are the sigil generator's (seed 1, 2026-10-03). Spell notes that name ratios or chord tones describe the earlier, hand-made recipes.

